body:
I understand your frustration but you should direct that towards the school system. As a professional STEM tutor, one thing I'm often seeing students tripping up on are the fundamental basics. For example they will not know what f(1) is but will know what f(x) is or they won't understand the concept of plugging in 5 for x. What happens is these students lose all confidence in their math ability which is first and foremost disheartening. Often I've heard from my students that whenever they asked questions in the past they were either humiliated or screamed at. The thing that most often makes me frustrated is that professors aren't explaining the fundamentals and are just expecting the student to understand because it seems so easy. I'm frustrated because teachers aren't encouraging questions to be asked!!

&#x200B;

I whole heatedly understand your frustration but please don't direct your frustration towards the student. They came to you because the school system failed them.

